Green. Summary of the fix in `src/main/java/com/acme/retry/RetryingClient.java` (production code only, public API unchanged):

```java
public <T> T execute(CheckedOperation<T> op) throws Exception {
  Exception last=null;
  for(int attempt=0; attempt<policy.maxAttempts(); attempt++) {
    try { return op.run(); } catch(Exception e) { last=e; }
  }
  throw last;
}
```

- **Max-attempt contract**: changed `attempt <= policy.maxAttempts()` to `attempt < policy.maxAttempts()` so `maxAttempts=3` means exactly 3 total calls, matching the documented contract (previously it made 4).
- **Terminal failure handling**: `throw last;` rethrows the original last exception (e.g. the `IOException`) instead of wrapping it in a synthetic `IllegalStateException("retry exhausted")`, so callers can catch the real cause.

`./verify.sh` now passes: `PASS RetryingClientTest`.

